<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phylăcē</span></b> ,
			ēs, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φυλακή</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A city of Thessaly</i>, <i>where
				Protesilaus reigned;</i> its ruins are near the mod. <i>Ghidek</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 9, 16, §
			32</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phylăcēis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, <i>adj. f.</i>,
				<i>Phylacian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">matres Phylaceides,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
					13, 35</span></i>
			.—<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phylăcēis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f. (acc.
			Phylaceida), <i>Laodamia</i>, <i>wife of
				Protesilaus</i>, <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 3,
			273</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phy-lăcēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>Phylacian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Laodamia</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					Tr. 5, 14, 39</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>Subst. plur.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phylăcaei</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., <i>the
				Phylacians</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 4, 9, 16, §
			34</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phȳ^lăcĭ-des</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Phyll-</span></b> ),
			ae, m., <i>Phylacides</i>,
			i. e. <i>Protesilaus</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. A. A. 2,
				356</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">respice Phylaciden,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib.
					3, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop.
					1, 19, 7</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A city of the Molossians in Epirus</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 45,
			26</span></i>.</div>
